# Title: Renamed ProcDump Execution
# ID: 4a0b2c7e-7cb2-495d-8b63-5f268e7bfd67
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2019-11-18
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.003
# Description: Detects the execution of a renamed ProcDump executable.
# This often done by attackers or malware in order to evade defensive mechanisms.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.pe.original_file_name:"procdump") OR (((process.command_line:* -ma * OR process.command_line:* -mp *)) AND (process.command_line:* /accepteula*))) AND NOT (((process.executable:*\\procdump.exe OR process.executable:*\\procdump64.exe OR process.executable:*\\procdump64a.exe))))
